  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nLogic: (1st number)² + (3rd number)² - (1st number + 3rd number) = 2nd number.\n\nGiven,\n\n(5, 62, 7)\n\n⇒ 5² + 7² - (5 + 7)\n\n⇒ 74 - 12 = 62.\n\nAnd, (8, 188, 12) \n\n⇒ 82 + 122 - (8 + 12)\n\n⇒ 208 - 20 = 188.\n\nNow, checking the options:\n\nOption 1) (10, 181, 9)\n\n⇒ 102 + 92 - (10 + 9)\n\n⇒ 181 - 19 = 162 ≠ 181.\n\n.Option 2) (6, 117, 19 )\n\n⇒ 62 + 192 - (6 + 19)\n\n⇒ 397 - 25 = 372 ≠ 117.\n\nOption 3) (11, 390, 13)\n\n⇒ 112 + 132 - (11 + 13)\n\n⇒ 190 - 24 = 166 ≠ 390.\n\nOption 4) (**7, 114, 9) **\n\n**⇒ 72 + 92 - (7 + 9)**\n\n⇒ 130 - 16 = 114.\n\n Hence, the correct option is \"Option 4\".",
